---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="General Terms & Conditions of Sale to Consumers" description="General terms and conditions for wine purchases from Domaine d'Aubigny. Delivery, payment, returns, age verification and legal information." lang="en">
  <style>
    .legal { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(56px, 12vw, 96px) var(--pad-x); }
    .legal__title { font-size: 36px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 500; margin: 32px 0 16px; }
    .legal h3 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; margin: 24px 0 12px; }
    .legal p, .legal li { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--body); margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .legal ul { margin-left: 24px; }
  </style>

  <section class="legal">
    <h1 class="legal__title">General Terms & Conditions</h1>
    <p><strong>Domaine d'Aubigny</strong> — Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Seller Identification</h2>
    <p>DOMAINE D'AUBIGNY, a simplified joint-stock company (Société par Actions Simplifiée) with share capital of EUR 70,620, registered office at Hameau d'Aubigny, 71510 Aluze, France, registered with the Chalon-sur-Saône Trade and Companies Register under number 841 534 803.</p>
    <p><strong>SIRET:</strong> 841 534 803 00033 | <strong>VAT:</strong> FR68841534803 | <strong>Phone:</strong> +33 3 85 44 76 76 | <strong>Email:</strong> contact@aubigny.wine</p>

    <h2>2. Scope</h2>
    <p>These terms govern the online sale of wines from Domaine d'Aubigny to consumers established in metropolitan France or in Member States of the European Union. Any wine purchase constitutes unreserved acceptance of these terms, which the buyer acknowledges having received and read.</p>

    <h2>3. Orders & Acceptance</h2>
    <p>Orders are placed electronically via shop.aubigny.wine. An order confirmation is sent to the email address provided. Domaine d'Aubigny reserves the right to refuse any order due to availability or non-compliance with its distribution policy.</p>

    <h2>4. Pricing</h2>
    <p>Prices are expressed in euros, all taxes included. They are valid on the day of order and may be changed at any time. Prices include French VAT (20%). For deliveries outside France, different VAT may apply.</p>

    <h2>5. Availability & Stock</h2>
    <p>Production at Domaine d'Aubigny comes from limited harvests. Volumes offered for sale depend on available vintages and cuvées. In case of unavailability of an ordered cuvée, the Estate will notify the buyer without delay and process a full refund.</p>

    <h2>6. Payment</h2>
    <p>Payment is made online in a secure environment at the time of order validation. Accepted payment methods are credit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express). Payment must be completed before order preparation and shipment.</p>

    <h2>7. Delivery</h2>
    <p>Orders are shipped in cases of 6 or 12 bottles. Delivery times are 3 to 5 business days in metropolitan France, and 5 to 10 days in the European Union, from order validation. Shipping costs are calculated by weight and destination. Domaine d'Aubigny uses a licensed carrier for alcohol transport.</p>

    <h2>8. Right of Withdrawal</h2>
    <p>In accordance with consumer law, you have 14 days from receipt to exercise your right of withdrawal, provided the bottle has not been opened or consumed. Returned bottles must be intact and properly packaged. Contact us at contact@aubigny.wine or call +33 3 85 44 76 76 to exercise this right. Return shipping costs are the buyer's responsibility.</p>

    <h2>9. Responsibility & Claims</h2>
    <p>Domaine d'Aubigny is responsible for the quality and compliance of wines delivered. In case of breakage during delivery, notify the carrier within two days and contact the Estate immediately. Any claims regarding defective bottles must be reported within 10 days of receipt. The Estate will process an exchange or refund based on the nature of the defect.</p>

    <h2>10. Age Verification</h2>
    <p>In compliance with alcohol regulations, the sale of alcoholic beverages is reserved for adults. By placing an order, you confirm being at least 18 years old. The carrier may request identification at delivery.</p>

    <h2>11. Personal Data</h2>
    <p>Personal data provided with your order is processed confidentially and used solely for order management and delivery. Data is not shared with third parties without prior consent. Domaine d'Aubigny complies with GDPR regulations.</p>

    <h2>12. Modification of Terms</h2>
    <p>Domaine d'Aubigny reserves the right to modify these terms at any time. Terms applicable to an order are those in effect on the date of order validation.</p>

    <h2>13. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by French law. In case of dispute, competent courts are those of the Chalon-sur-Saône jurisdiction.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
